  "conclusions": [
    "Observed SOC mismatch is explained by Android restoring a stale shutdown UI SOC of100 while actual gauge SOC was87.",
    "Android subsequently reported Full after a300-second UI-full timer at raw SOC90; battery current still indicated charging and displayed FV remained4490mV. Android Full is not equivalent to electrical termination in this observation.",
    "No evidence of NixOS overvoltage from this incident; inspected normal and FFC limits match the running stock Android device tree.",
    "This read-only investigation is not an exhaustive electrical safety certification or a new full-cycle acceptance test. No percentage scaling, calibration reset, gauge writes or charging-limit changes were made."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "No simultaneous independent voltmeter measurements.",
    "No new paired Android/NixOS full-charge cycle with identical charger and temperature.",
    "Android learned capacity and ADSP-reported NixOS charge_full differ; not enough evidence to attribute that difference to a calibration defect."
  ],
